==================================================
TECHNICAL PRINCIPLES
==================================================

- Avoid giant enums for all character states.
- Prefer orthogonal state dimensions.
- State authority belongs to the relevant system.
- SaveGame should use explicit structs/snapshots.
- Debug commands via FAutoConsoleCommand / debug subsystem.
- Compile success != package success != runtime success.
- Telemetry should be event-based.
- Unreal analytics layer + consent gate + GameAnalytics can be useful later.
- Steam is not a general telemetry backend.
- Do not build systems before the prototype proves they are needed.

Core architecture rule:
“Architecture should support the future, but implementation should solve the current problem.”

